# The suites of tools/suite.list in groups of similar length: one CI job per group (.github/workflows/ci.yml, matrix
# gruppo) and one Linux clone per group in the parallel run (tools/suite-parallelo.sh). Line: <group> <entry>, the
# entry spelled as in tools/suite.list. `tools/suite.sh --gruppo <k>/<n>` refuses (exit 2) a file whose groups are not
# 1..n, an entry of suite.list in no group or in two, an entry here that is not in suite.list.
# Inside a group the suites run in the order of suite.list.
# 1.8.0 (CI): five groups instead of three, balanced on the seconds of the first CI of 1.8.0 (the longer of its two
# runs, Linux · macOS): group 1 ≈ 462 · 676 s, group 2 ≈ 408 · 673, group 3 ≈ 464 · 695, group 4 ≈ 509 · 676,
# group 5 ≈ 604 · 582. The oracle alone is the longest suite (462 · 676 s).
# tools/esempi-equiv.test.sh (the expected outputs, and their strict checks with MAAT_ATTESE_RICHIESTE) is in group 4.
# A suite red only in the parallel run goes in a group of its own (docs/TESTING-harness.md, «The parallel run»).

# group 1: the oracle
1 tools/oracolo.test.sh

# group 2: the driver, the plan
2 driver
2 guard
2 plan-check
2 bash-node

# group 3: the phases
3 run-phase
3 finalize
3 maat-doctor
3 phase-events
3 tools/suite.test.sh

# group 4: the resume table, the messages, the public examples (expected outputs)
4 cycle-state
4 messages
4 tools/esempi-equiv.test.sh
4 gates

# group 5: the WSL tools, all the short ones
5 counterproof
5 test-fast
5 spazi
5 comandi-equivalenza
5 maat-paths
5 maat-config
5 nomi_test
5 transcript
5 ciclo-worktree
5 context-pack
5 cycle-report
5 harness-merge
5 stop-hook
5 blocks-independent
5 test-review-surface
5 genericita
5 senza-wsl
5 session-start
5 phase-usage
5 vitest-classify
